# Zero divisor of x-a has degree [F:K(x)]

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.degree_eq_finrank_adjoin_of_eq_max_ord_sub_algebraMap`
(`1781cf32-200c-5754-a230-e31ecb0c4e36`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `c90ac65a-83dd-5dcf-b598-ad7f9519bc1f`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero $f \in
F$ admits a finitely supported divisor $P$ with $P(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v f$ at every place and
$\deg P = 0$; each residue field $v.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is finite over $K$; and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is
free of rank $1$ over $F$. Here a place $v$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing
$\operatorname{im}(K \to F)$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, with
$\operatorname{ord}_v f = -\log v(f)$ for the adic valuation of the associated height-one prime.
Assume also that $\mathrm{LSpace}\,0 = \{f : v(f) \le 1 \text{ for all } v\}$ is finite-dimensional
over $K$. Let $x \in F$ be transcendental over $K$, with $F$ finite-dimensional over the
intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$, let $a \in K$, and let $D$ be a finitely supported
$\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on places with $D(v) = \max(0, \operatorname{ord}_v(x - a))$ for all
$v$, i.e. the divisor of zeros of $x - a$. Then $\deg D = \sum_v D(v)\cdot \deg v$ equals $[F :
K(x)]$, viewed in $\mathbb{Z}$.

This is the standard statement that the fibre of the map $x : X \to \mathbb{P}^1$ over a rational
point $a \in K$, counted with multiplicities and residue degrees, has size the degree $[F : K(x)]$;
it is the companion, over a finite point, of the corresponding statement for the pole divisor of
$x$. It is used in counting places with prescribed behaviour over an algebraically closed base
field, where every place has degree $1$.

